# `#if` and a compile-time loop decide while building. One that reads a
# parameter, known only at run time, is refused where it reads it, and never
# turns into a run-time `if` or `loop`: `#if n > 3` is E0989, and a body
# `#loop x in xs` (which `jet fmt` writes `#run { loop x in xs -> … }`) is
# E0640.
fixture: ComptimeNoSilentFallbackIfAndLoop.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet check source0/main.jet --json
exit: nonzero
json: stdout doc $.reports has {"code":"E0989","line":2}
step: jet check source1/main.jet --json
exit: nonzero
json: stdout doc $.reports has {"code":"E0640","line":4}
